{
  "id": "26920_jizokusuru",
  "headword": "{持続|じぞく}する",
  "reading": "じぞくする",
  "romaji": "jizokusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to continue; to persist; to sustain",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to continue; to persist; to sustain",
      "explanation": "For a state, condition, or activity to keep going over a period of time without interruption. Can be used both intransitively (something persists) and transitively (to sustain something)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26920_jizokusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{痛|いた}みが{三日|みっか}{持続|じぞく}した。",
      "english": "The pain persisted for three days.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26920_jizokusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{経済|けいざい}{成長|せいちょう}を{持続|じぞく}させることが{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "It is important to sustain economic growth.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26920_jizokusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{集中力|しゅうちゅうりょく}を{長時間|ちょうじかん}{持続|じぞく}するのは{難|むずか}しいので、{適度|てきど}に{休憩|きゅうけい}を{取|と}ろう。",
      "english": "It's hard to sustain concentration for long hours, so let's take breaks at appropriate intervals.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Emphasizes maintaining a state or activity over time. Commonly used in discussions about sustainability, durability, and endurance. The noun form {持続|じぞく} is extremely common as a modifier.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {持続|じぞく}{可能|かのう}な: sustainable\n- {持続|じぞく}{的|てき}な: continuous; sustained\n- {持続|じぞく}{力|りょく}: staying power; endurance\n- {持続|じぞく}{時間|じかん}: duration\n- {効果|こうか}が{持続|じぞく}する: the effect lasts\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {続|つづ}く: to continue — the basic, everyday word for continuation\n- {継続|けいぞく}する: to continue — emphasizes deliberate, ongoing effort to keep something going\n- {維持|いじ}する: to maintain — focuses on keeping something at its current level or state",
